 "caption": "Programs per suspicion score, honest in grey and backdoored in red, on a log scale so small counts show. The shaded region is what a requested 2% budget audits when only scores above the cutoff count. Sonnet gives 91% of honest programs one score; Haiku xhigh 54%.",
 "notes": [
  "Random tie-breaking fixes fairness, not sample size. At 500 honest programs a 1% budget still rests on 5 of them. The other fixes are a 0 to 100 scale (P15, P08) and more honest programs."
